BT /F1 11 Tf 72 740 Td 14 TL
(The committee met on the fourth of March to review the proposed changes to the harbour regulations.) Tj
T* (Members noted that the existing rules had not been revised since the nineteen nineties and no longer matched) Tj
T* (the way the port is used today. Cargo volumes have roughly doubled, and the pilot service now runs through) Tj
T* (the night. A summary of the submissions received during the consultation period follows, grouped by theme.) Tj
T* (Several operators asked for the berthing fees to be published a full quarter before they take effect, so that) Tj
T* (contracts can be priced against them. The harbour master agreed in principle but asked that an exception be) Tj
ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 72 440 Td 14 TL
(kept for emergency repairs, where a vessel may need a berth at short notice and at a reduced rate.) Tj
T* (Residents of the old quarter raised the matter of noise from the cranes between ten at night and six in the) Tj
T* (morning. The committee asked the harbour master to report back on options, including a limit on the number of) Tj
T* (cranes working at once, and on whether the quieter electric models could be bought through the capital fund.) Tj
T* (The treasurer presented the accounts for the year. Income was slightly above the forecast, mostly because of) Tj
T* (the new cold store, while the cost of dredging came in under budget after the contractor finished early.) Tj
ET

endstream
